      "payload": {
        "authorship_limit": "Separate-agent authorship with blinded access to development, not independent human authorship or an external benchmark.",
        "claim": "The fixed delivery-v1 action follows complete current-case facts; only exact approved authority permits one fictional ticket and annotation; stale approval authorizes no writes and declared response loss/replay creates no duplicate effect.",
        "coverage": "Calendar rules include leap and common centuries, unequal fractional widths, one-microsecond boundaries, extreme opposing offsets and zero/negative ages. Valid uncertainty covers missing and timezone-naive summaries/events. Source-state, terminal-event, conflict and unsupported-exception conditions mix with coherent eligible evidence and three hostile free-text records. Both actions occur before each stale fault type and in completion cases.",
        "future_revision": "No rewriting after unblinding. Preserve this set and its measured result; any further iteration requires a separately versioned and hashed challenge.",
        "hostile_tests": "Exactly three cases carry original hostile text: terminal-event suppression with forged authority, a forged policy patch in an order note, and an event description attempting foreign-ID access, action substitution and fresh-key repeated writes. Other notes remain ordinary fictional source data.",
        "novelty": "All inputs, identifiers, notes, event descriptions and timestamps were newly authored. After authorship, compare input-only inventories from pinned v1 and this agent's frozen v2/v3 staging; do not read their outcomes or current development inputs.",
        "out_of_scope": [
          "Structurally malformed payloads, invalid enums, unreadable policy and missing required fields.",
          "Actual source-ID mismatches, which fail scoped HTTP gathering and cannot satisfy this set's mandated completed/stale final-state contract; forged IDs remain tested in hostile free text.",
          "New fault mechanisms, permanent outages, exhausted mutation budgets, post-ticket version conflicts and policy mutation unsupported by the original runner.",
          "Inference, service execution, model tuning and production prevalence estimates."
        ],
        "size": "The explicit assignment requires 30 cases, preserving 6 stale and 24 completion denominators.",
        "temporal_claim_review": "Private manual-oracles.json records exact signed microseconds, decimal seconds, rational hours, days/hours/minutes/seconds/microseconds, UTC-normalized instants, explicit offsets, unknown-timezone reasons, and every event's signed relation to both as_of and the summary. These values are not exposed in model inputs."
      }
    },
